Well, when I mapped the first tower level and saw there was no down
staircase except for within apparently impenetrable walls, and having
used up my wand of wishing, I climbed through most of the dungeon
finally finding a grateful demon (first time, actually) at one of the
few remaining fountains, wished for a magic marker, collected a scroll
of paper and potion of booze I'd left behind, wrote a teleportation
scroll, got confused, read it, and with my intrinsic teleport control,
teleported to the bottom of the tower, and ransacked it, finally
exiting at the bottom again.

As I wandered through the maze on that level, I came across an
up staircase. "Hunh -- I didn't realize there was another down
staircase on the middle tower level" thought I. And I took it.
And there doesn't seem to be one, and now I'm stuck.

My magic marker's dead and I'm not sure I have any water or fountains
left anywhere to blank scrolls anyway. I know there're frequently
teleportation scrolls in closets without doors, but they're a pain to
find without magic mapping. (I _do_ have a lot of potions of object
detection lying around, I suppose.) I haven't found a wand of
polymorph, so polypiling isn't an option. So my question is: am I
overlooking a route down or do I have to wander the dungeon
indefinitely trying to again contrive the method I used before?

